{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfXUU5TmH5sJimtCsMeif","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Right unit for the rule.** The normalization logic lives in a dedicated `AddressNormalizer` rather than being inlined into either `NormalizeOwnerAddress` (the store-side step) or `HouseholdKey` (the compare-side). This directly mirrors the existing `HouseholdKey` pattern of \"one shared definition so the two call sites cannot drift apart,\" and the spec explicitly requires the same normalized form at both storage and comparison — so a single shared helper is the natural home. It avoids turning `HouseholdKey` into a catch-all for all address concerns.\n\n- **No harmful duplication.** `HouseholdKey` keeps its own private `normalize` for *last name* (collapse + case-insensitive) and delegates *address* to `AddressNormalizer` (collapse + upper + abbreviation expansion). These are genuinely different rules, so the small whitespace-collapsing overlap is not worth extracting — doing so would be over-abstraction.\n\n- **Idiomatic OfficeFloor wiring.** `NormalizeOwnerAddress` is a thin single-public-method function class that mutates the shared `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` in place — exactly the \"Apply mutates in place, later steps see the change\" idiom in AGENTS.md. Naming (`NormalizeOwnerAddress`, verb + entity) fits the `Validate`/`Apply`/`Build` family.\n\n- **Correct step ordering and governance.** Inserting `normalizeAddress` between `validate` and `require` means the blank-after-normalization check and both household comparisons all see the canonical form, satisfying the behavioural change without reordering surprises. `govern: [ transaction ]` matches its neighbours.\n\n- **Docs kept in sync.** The `HouseholdKey` Javadoc was updated to point at `AddressNormalizer` rather than left describing the old inline rule, and both new classes carry clear intent-level comments (including the rationale for keeping the helper out of the function class).\n\nThe re-application of `AddressNormalizer.normalize` inside `HouseholdKey` on already-normalized values is idempotent and reads as reasonable defensiveness, not a smell. A maintainer of this codebase would find the shape natural."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11168,"cache_read_input_tokens":11787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11168},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20b5306a-df7f-46b2-beed-b9c260beaf97","uuid":"63a966d6-2bba-412c-a257-affe4df4d462","timestamp":"2026-09-29T09:14:06.962Z","request_id":"req_011CfXUU4mc9yeZDNELyhLri"}
